		"title": "Quickstart",
		"section": "Start here",
		"heading": "When it doesn't work",
		"index": 6,
		"text": "When it doesn't work\n\n | What you see | What it means | Fix\n\n | 401 unauthorized | No usable credential. The message guesses at what you sent — it recognises a URL, an OpenAI-style sk- key, and a webhook secret by shape. | Check the header is authorization: Bearer and the key starts itsuki_live_.\n\n | 403 insufficient_scope | The key is valid but lacks the scope for this call. Saving needs memory:write. | Use a key with write scope. Keys carry both scopes unless you asked for otherwise.\n\n | 400 unknown_parameter | A field name the endpoint does not accept. The message names it and suggests the nearest match. | Fix the spelling. If there is no near match, the message lists every accepted field.\n\n | 404 not found | Routes match exactly — /v1/save/ with a trailing slash is not /v1/save. | Drop the trailing slash.\n\n | 429 too_many_requests | A rate bucket tripped. Saving allows 60 per minute; the body names the bucket. | Honour retry-after rather than sleeping a fixed amount. See Rate limits.\n\n | 409 idempotency_conflict | You reused an idempotencyKey for different content. | Mint a new key. The same key with the same content is a safe replay and returns the original receipt.\n\nEvery response carries an x-request-id header. It ties your call to the server-side record without anyone reading your memory content, so quote it if you report a problem."
