		"title": "Connect Claude",
		"section": "Connect your tools",
		"heading": "2 · Verify the connection",
		"index": 2,
		"text": "2 · Verify the connection\n\nA successful add makes Claude list the connector with its tools — eleven of them. Do not stop there: ask for the identity tool, which answers the three questions a wrong setup gets wrong.\n\nUse the whoami tool and tell me what it says.\n\nConnected to Itsuki memory (server 0.7.0). Project: Personal. Scopes: memory:read, memory:write. Stored: 12 memories (9 facts, 3 pages), 24 events, 0 pending candidates.\n\nRead it as three checks:\n\n | Part | What it proves\n\n | Project | Which project this link is bound to. A link is permanently bound to the project it was created in and cannot read or write another. If the name is wrong, you made the link in the wrong project.\n\n | Scopes | What this connection may do. memory:read alone means Claude can recall but not save — the link's declared scopes are intersected with its creator's current project role on every request, so a role change narrows a live connector with nothing to revoke.\n\n | Stored | Live counts, straight from the database. Run it again after a save; if the numbers moved, the round trip works.\n\nOpening the MCP URL in a browser proves nothing. The endpoint speaks MCP JSON-RPC over POST — a browser GET is not a meaningful test of the link. The whoami tool is."
