		"text": "3 · Save one fact, then recall it in a new chat\n\nRecall across conversations is the whole point, so test it across two conversations. In the chat you just verified:\n\nSave this to itsuki: I prefer concise project updates.\n\nClaude may ask you to approve the write the first time. The tool answers with a receipt, and Claude relays it:\n\nWhat project-update style do I prefer?\n\nThe tool hands Claude the recalled memory itself, not a status line, so the model can answer directly from it:\n\nRelevant memory for this user:\n\nProject updates — preference\n- prefers concise project updates\n\nIf the recall comes back empty seconds after the save, that is timing rather than failure: extraction finishes in the background. Ask again, or ask Claude to run list_memories to see what actually landed."
