		"index": 4,
		"text": "What the connector gives Claude\n\n | Tool | What Claude uses it for\n\n | recall_memory | Meaning-based lookup. The tool's text result is the recalled context itself.\n\n | save_memory | One durable fact you stated, in your words.\n\n | save_conversation | Several turns at once, when a discussion produced lasting decisions.\n\n | list_memories · get_memory | Browse and open what is stored, newest first, without leaving the chat.\n\n | update_memory · memory_history · rollback_memory | Correct a memory against its exact current revision, read its history, restore an earlier revision as a new forward one.\n\n | delete_memory · delete_all_memories | Guarded erasure. Bulk deletion previews first and destroys nothing without an explicit confirmation.\n\n | whoami | Identity, scopes, bound project, live counts.\n\nFull input schemas are in MCP tools. Deletion is a separate capability from writing: a connector whose creator is a project member, not an admin, gets \"Forbidden: your project role does not allow deleting memories.\" even though the tools are listed."
