		"heading": "When it doesn't work",
		"index": 6,
		"text": "When it doesn't work\n\n | What you see | What it means | Fix\n\n | \"That is an API key, not an MCP link…\" | You pasted an API key into the connector URL. The server re-checks the token as an API key purely so it can name the mistake. | Mint an MCP link: Get started → Claude → Create link. API keys travel in an Authorization: Bearer header and never in a URL.\n\n | \"That MCP link is revoked, expired, or not an MCP token.\" | The key behind the link was deleted, or the URL was truncated on the way in. | Create a fresh link and update the connector. Deleting a key stops it working immediately.\n\n | The connector is saved, but Claude has no memory tools in this chat | A saved connector stays off until enabled per chat. | + → Connectors → switch on itsuki. Repeat in each new conversation.\n\n | No Add custom connector option | On Team and Enterprise, custom connectors are added for the organization, not by individual members. | An Owner or Primary Owner adds it. Everyone else then enables it per chat.\n\n | No connector settings at all, on a phone | The mobile apps cannot add connectors. | Add it in a computer browser once; it is then available on mobile.\n\n | Claude answers the question but never calls a tool | By design — the host model chooses when tools run. | Ask explicitly (\"save that to itsuki\"), or add the standing instructions above.\n\n | \"You're sending requests very quickly — wait a few seconds and try again.\" | A rate bucket tripped for this credential. It arrives as a readable sentence so the model can relay it rather than breaking the turn. | Wait, then retry. See Rate limits.\n\n | whoami names a project you did not expect | The link is bound to the project it was created in, permanently. | Switch to the right project in the app, create a link there, and replace the connector's URL.\n\n | whoami reports Scopes: memory:read only | The role of whoever created the link no longer permits writing, so the write tools refuse with insufficient_scope. | Restore the role, or have someone with write access create the link.\n\nUse one link per tool. Each connector holding its own credential is the whole rotation story: delete one from API Keys and only that connector stops, with nothing else to reconfigure. Claude's UI, plan gating and beta status are Anthropic's to change — their guide is the authority if a screen here no longer matches.\n\nMCP toolsEvery tool this connector exposes, with its inputs and guarantees.Capture rulesDecide what Itsuki is allowed to keep before Claude sends it.Connect ChatGPTThe same memory through a workspace MCP app.Authentication & keysWhy an MCP link is not an API key, and what a role change narrows."
