		"section": "Connect your tools",
		"heading": "Connect ChatGPT",
		"index": 0,
		"text": "Connect ChatGPT\n\nA custom MCP app in your ChatGPT workspace that saves durable facts to Itsuki as you talk and reads them back in a later chat.\n\nThis is gated by OpenAI, not by Itsuki. Full MCP write actions are a beta limited to ChatGPT Business and Enterprise/Edu on the web. Free, Plus and Pro accounts cannot run them, and a Pro custom app is read/fetch only. Custom MCP apps are web-only, and agent mode does not use them. Screen names and permissions move while a beta is open, so OpenAI's developer mode and full MCP connectors guide is the authority for anything on their side of this page.\n\nThe read/fetch limit is worth understanding rather than working around. A read-only custom app expects a server to publish tools named search and fetch. Itsuki's MCP server publishes eleven tools and none of them are those — the read side is recall_memory, list_memories and get_memory. So a read/fetch-only app connected here has nothing it knows how to call. The account-type requirement is a hard prerequisite, not a nicety.\n\nBefore you start- A ChatGPT workspace on Business or Enterprise/Edu, and workspace-admin access to it. Enabling developer mode and publishing an app are both admin actions.\n- An Itsuki account whose project role can create keys. If yours cannot, Get started shows \"Your role cannot create project keys.\" where the button belongs — see Projects & teams.\n- A desktop browser for both halves. ChatGPT's mobile apps have no custom-app flow, and Itsuki shows an MCP link exactly once."
