		"heading": "What to expect",
		"index": 6,
		"text": "What to expect\n\n- Writes are asynchronous. A save is accepted immediately and finishes processing in the background, so a recall issued in the same breath may not see it yet.\n\n- Every write is scoped to one end user. user_id selects an isolated memory space; there is no shared default.\n\n- Deleting by source is exact. Pass the same source you wrote with, and only those memories go.\n\nEvery package on this page was published with signed build provenance and exercised against https://itsuki.app from its registry bytes — installed from PyPI or npm, run against production, and cleaned up to zero."
