		"heading": "JavaScript SDK",
		"index": 0,
		"text": "JavaScript SDK\n\nInstall the client, save a fact from a Node script, wait for it to settle, and read it back — then keep this page for the full method surface, the real retry numbers, and the one error class behind every failure.\n\nBefore you start- Node.js 18 or newer. The client uses the built-in fetch, AbortController and node:crypto, and declares engines.node: \">=18\". Older runtimes are not supported.\n- An API key. Create one under Setup → API Keys in the app, or follow the Quickstart. Keep it on a server — this client is not built for browser code.\n- An ESM entry point: a package.json with \"type\": \"module\", or a file named .mjs. The package ships ESM only, with no CommonJS build."
