		"index": 9,
		"text": "When it doesn't work\n\n | What you see | What it means | Fix\n\n | A new page on every save of the same chat | No conversationId and no threadId was sent, so there was no key to converge on. | Send a stable conversationId. Each distinct batch without one is a legitimate separate page and cannot be merged after the fact.\n\n | No conversation_page field at all on a 200 | The save was a direct save, not mode: \"conversation\"; or it was refused before the page half ran (idempotency conflict, backpressure). | Check command_mode — a conversation save reports conversation_collect.\n\n | {\"skipped\": \"pages_off_by_rule\"} | The project is set to build the graph only. | Settings → Memory extraction → Conversation pages, choose Auto — build Conversation pages, then Save changes.\n\n | {\"skipped\": \"conversation_page_advance_limit\"} | The page holds its maximum of 200 linked batches. | Move to a new conversation id. The existing page stays readable and correctable.\n\n | An update section is missing, and older ones read \"N earlier updates trimmed for size\" | The 24,000-character body cap was reached; oldest sections trim first. | Nothing is lost from the record — the batches remain linked to the page. Start a new conversation id for a long-running thread.\n\n | 428 precondition_required | The PATCH carried no revision, or an If-Match that was not a revision ETag. | Re-read the page and send If-Match: \"r<revision>\" or expectedRevision.\n\n | 412 stale_revision | A background advance or another editor moved the page first. Your write was not applied. | Reload, review the newer body, then retry. In the app: \"This conversation page changed while you were editing.\" — your draft is kept, and Load latest for review shows what changed.\n\n | 400 invalid_field | You sent a field a page does not accept — key_points and related_concepts are not editable. | Send only title, short_summary, or full_markdown. The error names the allowed set.\n\n | 404 revision_unavailable on a restore | That revision was never recorded, or was removed by a delete, a retention pass, or a project purge. | Restore a revision the history endpoint still lists.\n\n | Later saves no longer change the body | You edited full_markdown yourself, so the fence pins it against automatic rewriting. | Expected. Roll back to a machine-written revision to let advances resume.\n\n | A page you edited is refused with 409 object_archived | Archived memories leave recall and become read-only. | Restore it before editing.\n\nPOST /v1/saveThe conversation door in full, and every field on its response.MCP toolssave_conversation, its arguments, and the page_id it hands back.Corrections, history, and rollbackThe revision contract behind every page edit and advance.How recall worksWhere pages sit in the ranked, bounded context block."
